From: MilkFlint <milkflint@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: estimate voice frames as unaggregated again

ieee80211_tx_dequeue() asks for the airtime of a station's frame as
aggregated on every AC but voice, which drivers send one frame per PPDU.
360-mac80211-factor-out-part-of-ieee80211_calc_expected_.patch moved the
estimate into ieee80211_rate_expected_tx_airtime() but passed "aggregated"
for every frame, so a voice frame is charged a share of an A-MPDU's
preamble instead of a whole one: at HE80 MCS 9 2SS about 10 us instead of
about 55 us for 1500 bytes. AQL then lets several times the voice
airtime it means to into the hardware queue.

Pass the caller's ampdu flag on.

---
--- a/net/mac80211/airtime.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/airtime.c
@@ -827,7 +827,7 @@ u32 ieee80211_calc_expected_tx_airtime(struct ieee8021
 		u32 duration;
 
 		duration = ieee80211_rate_expected_tx_airtime(hw, tx_rate, ri,
-							      band, true, len);
+							      band, ampdu, len);
 		duration /= 1024;
 
 		return max_t(u32, duration, 4);
